{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Quotient.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Submodule.Map","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementLevel"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.gradedTrace_exists_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.gradedTrace_exists_unique","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.lean#L100-L129","doc":"**Graded Markov trace from the GS filtration (derived).**\n\nFor each level `ℓ` there is a **unique** `R`-linear trace\n\n  tr_{M,ℓ} : (J^ℓ / J^{ℓ+1}) → R\n\nsuch that `tr_{M,ℓ} ∘ π_ℓ = tr_M|_{J^ℓ}` on representatives — i.e.\n`tr_{M,ℓ}(π_ℓ x) = tr_M x` for every `x ∈ J^ℓ`.\n\n**Existence** is `Submodule.liftQ` of `tr_M|_{J^ℓ}` along the\nfiltration-respecting vanishing (`s.filtration_respecting`).\n**Uniqueness** is the universal property of the quotient: a linear\nmap out of `J^ℓ / J^{ℓ+1}` is determined by its values on\nrepresentatives.  Both are produced here, not assumed — no `sorry`,\nno axiom, no projected field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.gradedKer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.gradedKer","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.lean#L95-L98","doc":"The submodule `J^{ℓ+1}` viewed inside `J^ℓ` (the kernel along which\n`tr_M|_{J^ℓ}` descends to `J^ℓ / J^{ℓ+1}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.filtration_respecting","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.filtration_respecting","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.lean#L86-L86","doc":"**Filtration-respecting** (the legitimate input, not the\nconclusion): `tr_M` vanishes on `J^{ℓ+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.trace","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The Markov trace `tr_M : H_n(R, q) → R` as a linear functional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.filtration_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.filtration_mono","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.lean#L81-L81","doc":"`J^{ℓ+1} ⊆ J^ℓ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.filtration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.filtration","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.lean#L79-L79","doc":"The descending GS-filtration `J^ℓ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.module","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.module","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.addCommGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.addCommGroup","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.M","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.M","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.lean#L75-L75","doc":"The ambient `R`-module (the Hecke algebra). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.mk","kind":"ctor","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration","kind":"structure","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GradedMarkovTraceFromGSFiltration.lean#L60-L86","doc":"**GS-filtration data for the graded Markov trace.**\n\nBundles the genuine *inputs* of `prop:graded-markov-trace-from-gs-filtration`:\n\n* `M` — the ambient `R`-module (the Hecke algebra `H_n(R, q)`),\n* `filtration ℓ = J^ℓ` — the descending two-sided GS-filtration,\n* `filtration_mono` — `J^{ℓ+1} ⊆ J^ℓ`,\n* `trace = tr_M` — the Markov trace as an `R`-linear functional,\n* `filtration_respecting` — `tr_M` vanishes on `J^{ℓ+1}` (the\n  filtration-respecting property the descent needs).\n\nNo field encodes the descent conclusion: the induced trace and its\nuniqueness are *derived* by `gradedTrace_exists_unique` below. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:graded-markov-trace-from-gs-filtration","label":"prop:graded-markov-trace-from-gs-filtration","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/graded-markov-trace-from-gs-filtration.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}